pear"},{"surface":"பாய்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"பாய்ந்த","lemma":"பாய்ந்த","gloss":"pierced"}],"gloss":"pierced","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மார்பின்","parts":[{"text":"மார்பு","lemma":"mārpu","gloss":"chest"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"of the chest"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மடல்","parts":[{"text":"மடல்","lemma":"maṭal","gloss":"palmyra stem"}],"gloss":"palmyra stem"},{"surface":"வன்","parts":[{"text":"வன்","lemma":"வன்","gloss":"strong"}],"gloss":"strong","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"போந்தையின்","parts":[{"text":"போந்தை","lemma":"pōntai","gloss":"palmyra tree"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"like the palmyra tree"},{"surface":"நிற்கும்","parts":[{"text":"நில்","lemma":"nil","gloss":"to stand"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"increment"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"standing"},{"surface":"ஓர்க்கே","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"people"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"kku","gloss":"dative suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"to those people indeed"}]}],"literal":"Abundant water desiring cool agricultural tract's buffalo / resembling dark horns long excellent dry pod / green beans threshed chaff's stem heap / having calf wild cow sleeping small village's / plunder here we do not want, the gift indeed, fiber filtered / bud matured jar's toddy praising / water-ghat very much possessing water-hen giving birth / cool agricultural tract obtaining is indeed possible, sharp point / long spear pierced chest's / palmyra stem strong palmyra tree like standing to those indeed","translation":"We do not want to plunder this small village where wild cows with calves sleep on heaps of stalks from which green beans have been threshed, stalks that resemble the long, excellent dry pods of the dark-horned buffaloes that graze in the cool, well-watered fields. Instead, it is indeed possible to obtain as a gift the cool agricultural tracts where water-hens hatch their eggs near the water-ghats, by praising with matured jar-toddy filtered through fiber, those heroes who stand firm like strong-stemmed palmyra trees, their chests pierced by sharp-pointed long spears.","modern":"பெரிய நீர்நிலைகளில் மேயும் எருமைகளின் கரிய கொம்புகளைப் போன்ற, நீண்ட சிறந்த உலர்ந்த நெற்றுகளையுடைய பசுமையான பயறுகளை உதிர்த்த மிச்சமுள்ள தட்டுகளின் குவியலில், கன்றையுடைய காட்டுப் பசுக்கள் உறங்கும் இந்தச் சிறிய ஊரைக் கொள்ளையிட நாங்கள் விரும்பவில்லை. நார் கொண்டு அரிக்கப்பட்ட, மொட்டுகள் முதிர்ந்து பக்குவப்பட்ட சாடித் கள்ளைப் பருகி வாழ்த்தி, நீர்நிலைகளின் துறைகளில் கம்புள் பறவைகள் முட்டையிட்டு இனப்பெருக்கம் செய்யும் குளிர்ந்த வயல்நிலங்களைப் பரிசாகப் பெறுவது சாத்தியமே. கூர்மையான முனையையுடைய நீண்ட வேல்கள் பாய்ந்த மார்போடு, மடல் பொருந்திய வலிமையான பனைமரத்தைப் போல நிமிர்ந்து நிற்கும் வீரர்களுக்கு அதுவே தகுதியானது.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Veṭci tiṇai (cattle-raiding/warfare) and the theme of Iṇṭāṭṭu (praising the heroes). The poet or bard speaks about the valor of the warriors of a small village. He states that they do not wish to plunder this small, peaceful village where wild cows sleep on threshed bean-stalks. Instead, they seek to obtain fertile, cool agricultural lands as gifts by praising the brave warriors. These warriors stand firm like strong palmyra trees, even when their chests are pierced by sharp spears in battle. The imagery of the peaceful village contrasting with the fierce battlefield highlights the heroism and honor of the warriors.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}